{
  "name": "athletics-qualifies-within-on-a-lapped-course",
  "why": "`qualifies_within` on four laps of 2 500 m, bound to the finish at 10 000 m. Every lap line produces `finished`, so a finish is not any `finished` but one at the place the rule is bound to. One runner runs all four laps in 45:00 and qualifies. One stops after two laps at 20:00 with no `withdrew` — two `finished`, inside fifty minutes, and never at the finish — and does not. One withdraws after three laps, and one runs all four in 55:00: neither qualifies.",
